# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ISR Systems · Environment configuration template
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values.
# .env.local is gitignored — safe for secrets.
#
# Vite exposes only variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser bundle.
# Everything below is read at build time via import.meta.env.VITE_*.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Cesium Ion (photoreal profile only) ──────────────────────────────────
# Free tier at https://ion.cesium.com/tokens
VITE_CESIUM_ION_TOKEN=

# ── Mistral inference (Agent B narrative synthesis) ──────────────────────
# Scaleway Generative APIs, OpenAI-compatible endpoint
VITE_MISTRAL_ENDPOINT=
VITE_MISTRAL_MODEL=
VITE_MISTRAL_API_TOKEN=

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SOVEREIGN PROFILE — Danish data-provider credentials
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Only needed if you run with ?profile=sovereign in the URL, or set
# localStorage['isr:render_profile'] = 'sovereign'. Photoreal profile
# ignores everything below.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── SDFI · dataforsyningen.dk ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Single token for Kortforsyningen + Dataforsyningen APIs. Powers:
#   - SDFI GeoDanmark Ortofoto (spring, autumn)
#   - SDFI Skærmkortet (topografisk basiskort)
#   - DAGI vectors (kommuner, politikredse, regioner)
#
# Registration:
#   1. https://dataforsyningen.dk → click "Log ind" (top right)
#   2. Sign in with MitID (or create a free account with email)
#   3. Navigate to "Min side" → "Token"
#   4. Copy the 32-char hex token
#   5. Paste below
VITE_SDFI_TOKEN=

# ── DMI (Danmarks Meteorologiske Institut) ──────────────────────────────
# NO CREDENTIALS NEEDED. DMI Open Data is fully public since Dec 2025 —
# no signup, no api-key, no headers. Fair-use limit: 500 requests / 5s.
# Endpoint: https://opendataapi.dmi.dk
# APIs available (all free, all anonymous):
#   - Meteorological Observations (dmi_weather)
#   - Oceanographic Observations + Tidewater (dmi_oceanobs)
#   - Lightning Data (dmi_lightning)
#   - Radar Data STAC (dmi_radar_stac)
#   - Forecast Data STAC (dmi_forecast_stac)
#   - Forecast Data EDR (dmi_forecast_edr)
# No env var required.

# ── Datafordeler · datafordeler.dk (BBR + CVR) ───────────────────────────
# Powers:
#   - BBR (Bygnings- og Boligregistret) per-building lookups
#   - CVR (Central Business Register) company lookups
#
# Registration is a two-step flow (webbruger + tjenestebruger):
#
#   PART 1 — First-time setup (Selvbetjening portal):
#     1. https://datafordeler.dk/konto/log-paa-selvbetjening/
#     2. Log på Selvbetjening → MitID Erhverv (recommended for ISR
#        Systems ApS — makes the webbruger org-bound, not Lucas-bound)
#     3. In Administration: create a webbruger (username + password)
#
#   PART 2 — Add services to your webbruger:
#     4. https://selfservice.datafordeler.dk/ → log in with the
#        webbruger from step 3
#     5. Webbrugere → open your webbruger → Tjenester → Tilføj tjeneste
#     6. Add BBRPublic — FREE, INSTANT, no IP allow-list needed
#     7. To ALSO add HentCVRData: send an access request email to
#        cvrselvbetjening@erst.dk (Erhvervsstyrelsen). NOT self-service.
#        Include: services requested, environment, webbruger + tjeneste-
#        bruger names, source IPs (no IPv6). Free but needs manual review.
#
#   PART 3 — Programmatic access:
#     8. Under the same webbruger, create a Tjenestebruger (auto-
#        generated username + password) — this is the credential the
#        code uses for REST calls (NOT the webbruger creds).
#     9. Paste the tjenestebruger creds below as "username:password"
#        (literal colon between them — the code splits on it).
#
# NB: REST on Datafordeler is being phased out end-2026. GraphQL is the
# successor. Bridge-round demo is fine on REST.
VITE_DATAFORDELER_CREDS=

# ── openAIP (community airspaces GeoJSON) ────────────────────────────────
# Powers:
#   - Danish airspace class polygons (TMA, CTR, restricted, danger areas)
#   - "Is this drone in controlled airspace?" context for escalation
#
# Registration:
#   1. https://www.openaip.net → Sign up (free)
#   2. Settings → API keys → generate a new key
#   3. Paste below
#
# Community-curated (mirror of Eurocontrol EAD / AIXM 5.1). Fine for
# visualisation. NOT airworthiness-authoritative. Data refreshes every
# 28 days (AIRAC cycle).
VITE_OPENAIP_KEY=

# ── Vejdirektoratet Dataudveksleren (live traffic events) ────────────────
# Powers:
#   - Live road-traffic incidents + congestion + roadworks on DK highways
#   - Realistic ETA for response asset routing (politi, brand, ambulance)
#
# Registration:
#   1. https://du-portal-ui.dataudveksler.app.vd.dk/ → Register account
#   2. Themes → generate API subscription key
#   3. Paste below
#
# Free. DATEX II XML format. 5-min polling cadence recommended.
VITE_VEJDIREKTORATET_KEY=

# ── AIS proxy WebSocket URL (scripts/ais-proxy/ deployed on Scaleway) ────
# When empty, the frontend falls back to a mock AIS provider that emits
# synthetic ships along Danish sejlruter. Deploy scripts/ais-proxy/ to
# Scaleway (see its README.md) and paste the WSS URL below to switch to
# real DMA-sourced AIS traffic.
#   Example: wss://ais-proxy.functions.fnc.fr-par.scw.cloud/ships
VITE_AIS_WS_URL=

# ── ICAO iSTARS (Danish airspace NOTAMs) ─────────────────────────────────
# Powers:
#   - NOTAM feed (temporary airspace restrictions, closures, hazards)
#   - Naviair has no public NOTAM feed — ICAO iSTARS is the free path
#
# Registration:
#   1. https://applications.icao.int/dataservices → Sign up
#   2. Approve email → generate API key
#   3. Paste below
#
# Free tier: 100 requests/day. Paid tier for higher volume.
VITE_ICAO_ISTARS_KEY=

# ── DHM self-hosted terrain tiles (post-deploy) ──────────────────────────
# Set after building + hosting DHM quantized-mesh tiles via
# scripts/dhm-pipeline/ (Scaleway Object Storage or Azure Blob).
#   Example: https://isr-dhm-tiles.s3.fr-par.scw.cloud
VITE_DHM_TERRAIN_URL=

# ── Self-hosted 3D building tiles (post-deploy) ──────────────────────────
# Set after building + hosting 3D Tiles from CityGML via
# scripts/city-tiles-pipeline/. Sovereign profile only.
#   Example: https://isr-city-tiles.s3.fr-par.scw.cloud
VITE_CITY_TILES_URL=

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Notes
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# - DAWA reverse-geocode is public — no token needed, always works
# - DMI Open Data is public — no token needed, always works
# - All sovereign services are FREE for their standard tiers
# - Datafordeler restricted datasets (BBR-fortrolig, CPR, Ejendom) need
#   separate signed access agreements per dataset
